{"id":"por-t1-0004","lang":"por","tier":1,"slot":"count.nine","domain":2,"text_native":"nove","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Nine.","source_caption":"9","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Continuing the count.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Portuguese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Portuguese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"por-t1-0005","lang":"por","tier":1,"slot":"count.one","domain":2,"text_native":"um (masc.) / uma (fem.)","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"One.","source_caption":"1","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Counting from one upward in order, because a traveller counts by reciting rather than by arithmetic.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Portuguese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Portuguese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"por-t1-0006","lang":"por","tier":1,"slot":"count.seven","domain":2,"text_native":"sete","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Seven.","source_caption":"7","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Continuing the count.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Portuguese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Portuguese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"por-t1-0007","lang":"por","tier":1,"slot":"count.six","domain":2,"text_native":"seis","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Six.","source_caption":"6","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Continuing the count.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Portuguese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Portuguese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"por-t1-0008","lang":"por","tier":1,"slot":"count.ten","domain":2,"text_native":"dez","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Ten.","source_caption":"10","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The first number past the counting pattern in most of these languages.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Portuguese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Portuguese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"por-t1-0009","lang":"por","tier":1,"slot":"count.three","domain":2,"text_native":"três","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Three.","source_caption":"3","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Continuing the count.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Portuguese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Portuguese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"por-t1-0010","lang":"por","tier":1,"slot":"count.two","domain":2,"text_native":"dois (masc.) / duas (fem.)","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Two.","source_caption":"2","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Continuing the count.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Portuguese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Portuguese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"por-t1-0011","lang":"por","tier":1,"slot":"count.zero","domain":2,"text_native":"zero","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"None, zero.","source_caption":"0","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Zero is the answer that gets misheard most often, because the word for nothing and the word for a small quantity are often unrelated.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Portuguese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Portuguese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"por-t1-0012","lang":"por","tier":1,"slot":"price.bill","domain":3,"text_native":"A conta, por favor.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"The bill, please.","source_caption":"The check, please.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Where the word for bill and the word for receipt are the same word and neither is 'account'.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Portuguese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Portuguese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"por-t1-0013","lang":"por","tier":1,"slot":"price.card-ok","domain":3,"text_native":"Aceita cartão de crédito?","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Is card payment accepted?","source_caption":"Do you accept credit cards?","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The alternative to carrying cash, and the question that decides whether you are standing in a queue that moves.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Portuguese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Portuguese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"por-t1-0014","lang":"por","tier":1,"slot":"price.how-much","domain":3,"text_native":"Quanto custa isto?","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"How much is this?","source_caption":"How much is this?","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The most useful question in the tier, and the one people are most afraid to ask. It is not rude anywhere.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Portuguese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Portuguese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"por-t1-0015","lang":"por","tier":1,"slot":"price.too-cheap","domain":3,"text_native":"barato","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"It is cheaper in my country.","source_caption":"cheap","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Read as an accusation almost everywhere. Included because knowing that it is an accusation is worth more than being able to say it politely.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Portuguese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Portuguese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"por-t1-0016","lang":"por","tier":1,"slot":"price.too-expensive","domain":3,"text_native":"É demasiado caro.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"That is too expensive.","source_caption":"That's too expensive.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Used with the hand gesture that accompanies it. The gesture carries the meaning and the word confirms it.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Portuguese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Portuguese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"por-t1-0017","lang":"por","tier":1,"slot":"money.atm","domain":3,"text_native":"Onde há um Multibanco?","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Where is an ATM?","source_caption":"Where is an automatic teller machine (ATM)?","register":"neutral","direction":"understand","why":"Recognising rather than producing it: you will be shown the sign rather than expected to ask.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Portuguese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Portuguese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"por-t1-0018","lang":"por","tier":1,"slot":"money.change","domain":3,"text_native":"Pode trocar dinheiro para mim?","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Please change this into local money.","source_caption":"Can you change money for me?","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The word 'change' means both coins and alteration in several of these languages, and the wrong one is confusing.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Portuguese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Portuguese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"por-t1-0019","lang":"por","tier":1,"slot":"money.keep-change","domain":3,"text_native":"Fique com o troco!","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Please keep the change.","source_caption":"Keep the change!","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Refusing loose coins is often faster and always understood.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"attested","id":"Tatoeba por-en sentence pairs (CC BY 2.0 FR)","url":"https://tatoeba.org/en/downloads","licence":"CC BY 2.0 FR, some CC0","external_id":"2213850","author":"CK"},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"por-t1-0020","lang":"por","tier":1,"slot":"toilet.where","domain":12,"text_native":"Onde é o banheiro?","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Where is the toilet?","source_caption":"Where is the toilet?","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The most urgent question in this tier and the one every phrasebook leads with. In several languages the word is the only one a traveller needs for years.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"attested","id":"Tatoeba por-en sentence pairs (CC BY 2.0 FR)","url":"https://tatoeba.org/en/downloads","licence":"CC BY 2.0 FR, some CC0","external_id":"976274","author":"CK"},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"por-t1-0021","lang":"por","tier":1,"slot":"food.menu","domain":4,"text_native":"Posso ver a ementa, por favor?","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"The menu, please.","source_caption":"Can I look at the menu, please?","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"One question covers a whole meal. Most phrasebooks waste slots on individual dishes instead.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Portuguese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Portuguese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"por-t1-0022","lang":"por","tier":1,"slot":"food.no-meat","domain":4,"text_native":"Eu não como carne de porco.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"I do not eat meat.","source_caption":"I don't eat pork.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Saying it once at the start of the trip saves a refusal at the table, where it is awkward for both sides.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Portuguese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Portuguese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"por-t1-0023","lang":"por","tier":1,"slot":"food.water","domain":4,"text_native":"água","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Water, please.","source_caption":"water","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Refusing the water in a restaurant is a small discourtesy in several of these countries. This is how to ask for some instead.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Portuguese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Portuguese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"por-t1-0024","lang":"por","tier":1,"slot":"way.straight","domain":7,"text_native":"reto","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Go straight ahead.","source_caption":"straight ahead","register":"neutral","direction":"understand","why":"Recognised rather than produced.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Portuguese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Portuguese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"por-t1-0025","lang":"por","tier":1,"slot":"way.turn-left","domain":7,"text_native":"Vire à esquerda","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Turn left.","source_caption":"Turn left.","register":"neutral","direction":"understand","why":"Recognised rather than produced: you are the one being given directions far more often than giving them.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Portuguese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Portuguese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"por-t1-0026","lang":"por","tier":1,"slot":"way.turn-right","domain":7,"text_native":"Vire à direita","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Turn right.","source_caption":"Turn right.","register":"neutral","direction":"understand","why":"Recognised rather than produced.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Portuguese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Portuguese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"por-t1-0027","lang":"por","tier":1,"slot":"stay.checkout","domain":5,"text_native":"Quero fazer check out.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"I would like to check out, please.","source_caption":"I want to check out.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Said the morning before leaving, so the bill is not waiting at the desk while luggage is being gathered.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Portuguese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Portuguese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"por-t1-0028","lang":"por","tier":1,"slot":"stay.room","domain":5,"text_native":"Tenho uma reserva.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"I have a room booked.","source_caption":"I have a reservation.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The opening line at a front desk, and the word that gets you past it is the name on the booking.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"attested","id":"Tatoeba por-en sentence pairs (CC BY 2.0 FR)","url":"https://tatoeba.org/en/downloads","licence":"CC BY 2.0 FR, some CC0","external_id":"985188","author":"CK"},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"por-t1-0029","lang":"por","tier":1,"slot":"move.destination","domain":6,"text_native":"Leve-me para lá, por favor.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Please take me there.","source_caption":"Take me there, please.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Shown with a map or a written address while saying it. 'There' is the word the pages use; 'this address' is in none of them, and a slot phrased from imagination rather than from a caption is a slot that can never be filled.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Portuguese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Portuguese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"por-t1-0030","lang":"por","tier":1,"slot":"move.ticket","domain":6,"text_native":"Um ingresso, por favor.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"One ticket to","source_caption":"I'd like one ticket, please.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Ordering the number and the destination together, which is the whole transaction.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"attested","id":"Tatoeba por-en sentence pairs (CC BY 2.0 FR)","url":"https://tatoeba.org/en/downloads","licence":"CC BY 2.0 FR, some CC0","external_id":"8452218","author":"mailohilohi"},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"por-t1-0031","lang":"por","tier":1,"slot":"health.doctor","domain":9,"text_native":"Preciso de um médico.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"I need a doctor.","source_caption":"I need a doctor.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Short enough to say to anyone, which is the point — a phrase you cannot finish is a phrase that arrives too late.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Portuguese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Portuguese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"por-t1-0032","lang":"por","tier":1,"slot":"health.hospital","domain":9,"text_native":"Onde fica o hospital mais próximo?","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Where is the nearest hospital?","source_caption":"Where is the closest hospital?","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Asked of a passer-by rather than declared to a driver. The pages carry the question and not the instruction to be driven, which is a different conversation with a different person.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"attested","id":"Tatoeba por-en sentence pairs (CC BY 2.0 FR)","url":"https://tatoeba.org/en/downloads","licence":"CC BY 2.0 FR, some CC0","external_id":"7019247","author":"KoreanBeaver"},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"por-t1-0033","lang":"por","tier":1,"slot":"health.hurt","domain":9,"text_native":"Eu fui ferido.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"I have been injured.","source_caption":"I've been injured.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Declares the situation before being asked. Several of these languages change tense or register on the word for injury, and the flat version sounds like a complaint.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Portuguese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Portuguese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"por-t1-0034","lang":"por","tier":1,"slot":"help.dont-touch","domain":10,"text_native":"Não me toque!","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Do not touch me.","source_caption":"Don't touch me!","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Out loud and to a person, not shouted generally. Several of these languages treat it as an accusation, so it is a sentence to use deliberately.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Portuguese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Portuguese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"por-t1-0035","lang":"por","tier":1,"slot":"help.emergency","domain":10,"text_native":"É uma emergência.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"It is an emergency.","source_caption":"It's an emergency.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Changes how the next thirty seconds go. Two words, and in several of these languages it reaches a different set of responses than a request would.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Portuguese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Portuguese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"por-t1-0036","lang":"por","tier":1,"slot":"help.leave-me-alone","domain":10,"text_native":"Deixe-me em paz!","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Please leave me alone.","source_caption":"Leave me alone!","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Said firmly and quietly. Raising the volume is what turns it from a boundary into an incident in several of these cultures.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Portuguese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Portuguese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"por-t1-0037","lang":"por","tier":1,"slot":"help.lost","domain":10,"text_native":"Estou perdido. (masc.) / Estou perdida. (fem.)","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"I am lost.","source_caption":"I'm lost.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Asking a passer-by for help is a separate skill from reading a sign, and it uses different vocabulary in every one of these languages.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Portuguese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Portuguese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"por-t1-0038","lang":"por","tier":1,"slot":"help.phone","domain":10,"text_native":"Posso usar o seu telefone?","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Can I use your phone?","source_caption":"Can I use your phone?","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The most common thing a traveller needs that a phone provides, and asking a stranger for it is usually granted.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Portuguese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Portuguese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"por-t1-0039","lang":"por","tier":1,"slot":"help.police","domain":10,"text_native":"Vou chamar a polícia.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Please call the police.","source_caption":"I'll call the police.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Usually needs a phone, and in most places a local number rather than an international one.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Portuguese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Portuguese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"por-t1-0040","lang":"por","tier":1,"slot":"help.thief","domain":10,"text_native":"Pára! Ladrão!","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Stop, thief!","source_caption":"Stop! Thief!","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Loud, and aimed at a crowd rather than at one person. Included because the vocabulary exists and because it is the sentence that makes people nearby move.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Portuguese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Portuguese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
